    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero section-shell">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A private photo time machine for siblings</p>
          <h1>See them at<br><em>the same age.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-deck">At That Age finds the moment your older kid was exactly as old as your younger kid is today—then puts the photos side by side.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <span class="store-button" aria-label="Coming soon to the App Store">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17.1 12.5c0-2.9 2.4-4.3 2.5-4.4a5.3 5.3 0 0 0-4.2-2.3c-1.8-.2-3.5 1-4.4 1-.9 0-2.3-1-3.8-1-2 0-3.9 1.2-4.9 3-2.1 3.6-.5 9 1.5 11.9 1 1.4 2.1 3 3.7 2.9 1.5-.1 2.1-1 3.9-1s2.3 1 3.9 1c1.6 0 2.6-1.4 3.6-2.9a13 13 0 0 0 1.6-3.4 5 5 0 0 1-3.4-4.8ZM14.2 3.9A5 5 0 0 0 15.4.3a5.2 5.2 0 0 0-3.4 1.7 4.7 4.7 0 0 0-1.2 3.5 4.3 4.3 0 0 0 3.4-1.6Z"/></svg>
              <span><small>Coming soon to the</small>App Store</span>
            </span>
            <span class="compatibility">Made for iPhone · iOS 17+</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="trust-list" aria-label="Highlights">
            <li>Free daily comparisons</li>
            <li>No account</li>
            <li>No subscription</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="At That Age app showing two children side by side at the same age">
          <div class="age-note age-note-left">
            <span class="note-name">Lincoln</span>
            <span>4 years · 7 months</span>
          </div>
          <div class="phone phone-hero">
            <div class="phone-screen">
              <img src="/img/at-that-age-today.png" alt="The Today view in At That Age, with two sibling photo spaces side by side" width="1206" height="2622">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="age-note age-note-right">
            <span class="note-name">Isaac</span>
            <span>4 years · 7 months</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="moment-strip" aria-label="How the comparison works">
        <p><strong>Today:</strong> Isaac is 4 years, 7 months old.</p>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <p>Lincoln was that age <strong>665 days ago.</strong></p>
      </section>

      <section class="intro section-shell" id="how-it-works">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Your camera roll remembers</p>
          <h2>One age. Every kid.</h2>
          <p>Birthdays do the math. Your photo library supplies the memories. At That Age brings the right moments together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="step-number">01</span>
            <h3>Add your kids</h3>
            <p>Enter their names and birthdays. Optionally teach the app a few faces to improve its matches.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="step-number">02</span>
            <h3>Let it find the moment</h3>
            <p>The app searches nearby dates and ranks the best photos for each child—all on your iPhone.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="step-number">03</span>
            <h3>Look back together</h3>
            <p>Compare everyone side by side, try another age or date, and share the result with family.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature section-shell">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Not just today</p>
          <h2>Rewind to any age.</h2>
          <p>See everyone at six months old. Revisit this day three years ago. Or choose a date that matters to your family.</p>
          <p class="fine-print">Today and a fresh comparison are free each day. Choosing any age or date is a one-time unlock.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="phone-pair" aria-label="The Compare and Kids screens in the app">
          <div class="phone phone-back">
            <div class="phone-screen"><img src="/img/at-that-age-kids.png" alt="The Kids setup view in At That Age" width="1206" height="2622" loading="lazy"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="phone phone-front">
            <div class="phone-screen"><img src="/img/at-that-age-compare.png" alt="The Compare view for choosing a different age" width="1206" height="2622" loading="lazy"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy" id="privacy">
        <div class="privacy-inner section-shell">
          <div class="privacy-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><path d="M24 4 9 10v11c0 10.2 6.4 19.3 15 23 8.6-3.7 15-12.8 15-23V10L24 4Zm0 6.2 9 3.6V21c0 6.9-3.8 13.5-9 16.6-5.2-3.1-9-9.7-9-16.6v-7.2l9-3.6Zm-2.2 7.3v4h-2.3v9h9v-9h-2.3v-4a2.2 2.2 0 0 0-4.4 0Zm2.2-4a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v4h1.5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v11a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-11a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-11a1 1 0 0 1 1-1H20v-4a4 4 0 0 1 4-4Z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p>
            <h2>Your family photos stay in the family.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="privacy-copy">
            <p>Photo search and face matching happen on your iPhone using Apple’s Photos and Vision technologies.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>No developer-operated server</li>
              <li>No photo or face-data uploads</li>
              <li>No analytics or tracking</li>
              <li>No account to create</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="fine-print">Photos may download originals from your iCloud Photo Library when needed, just as they do in other photo apps. Your saved kids and face signatures are included in normal device backups.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="questions section-shell" id="questions">
        <div class="section-heading compact">
          <p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p>
          <h2>A few questions, answered.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Do I need to organize my photos first?</summary>
            <p>No. At That Age can search your whole library by date. For more accurate results, you can optionally teach it each kid’s face or point it to a Photos album.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does it upload my photos?</summary>
            <p>No. The app has no developer-operated server. Photo lookup and face matching run locally on your iPhone.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What is included for free?</summary>
            <p>You can always see today’s comparison plus one different comparison the app picks each day. Choosing any age or date is available as a one-time purchase.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I move my setup to another iPhone?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Export a small settings file containing names, birthdays, and taught face signatures, then AirDrop or import it on another iPhone. Your photos are never included in that file.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

